      "title": "M2.2 · TimeMap: tempo and meter changes round-trip",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "M2.2: a Sequence now carries its score's tempo and meter map (m5.TimeMap), so Score -> Sequence -> Score keeps tempo changes, time signatures and a pickup.\n\nInput: flute + cello. A one-quarter pickup, bars 1-2 in 3/4 at quarter = 72, bars 3-4 in 6/8 at dotted quarter = 60, bar 5 in 2/4 at quarter = 96.\n\nPress Run. Look at:\n1. Original score (top middle).\n2. Sequence Viewer: the notes at their times in ms. The eighths in 6/8 and the 2/4 bar are timed by their own tempos.\n3. Back to a score (right): Sequence to Score with bpm 0 now uses the Sequence's tempo map instead of estimating one tempo. It should match the original: the pickup (bar 0), 3/4 -> 6/8 -> 2/4, and the marks quarter = 72, dotted quarter = 60, quarter = 96 in the same places.\n\nTry: set bpm to 72 on Sequence to Score. That forces one tempo and keeps only the first time signature (3/4), so the later bars are re-barred: the old behaviour for Sequences without a map.\n\nThe M2.1 workflow (duo, 90 -> 120 BPM) now also comes back with both tempo marks."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
